== 2. Findings ==

F1r3 [Blocker] adversarial-testing: the F1r2 remediation covers the root and
each workspace but not the apps/ parent, where the suite still seeds
leak-prone folders. The sweep reads [REPO_ROOT, ...WORKSPACE_DIRS]
(oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:152; WORKSPACE_DIRS at :1335 holds apps/* and
packages/* workspaces, never apps/ itself), and makeLintProbe seeds
.oxlint-probe-* under apps/ (:1401), the class that the F1r2 blast radius
named. Live proof: apps/.oxlint-probe-R3STALE-iPK7Cx/probe.ts survived the
real beforeAll sweep while every covered class was removed. Honest impact:
no current gate step reads the apps/ parent one level (gates.sh:95 skips
dotfolders; adv 7 walks WORKSPACE_DIRS only, :1674), so the leak is
unremoved litter today, not a red gate. Fix owner Green, one line: add
path.join(REPO_ROOT, 'apps') to the sweep parent list. The r3 b pin flips.

F2r3 [Blocker] adversarial-testing: the sweep prefix '.oxlint-adv' is
broader than every seeded form, so the sweep deletes an untracked near-miss
folder that no test seeded. Every seeded name continues with '-' or a digit
(PROBE_DIR_PREFIXES at :135), but the match is
entry.name.startsWith('.oxlint-adv') (:156), which also matches
.oxlint-advisory and each similar name. Live proof: the seeded
.oxlint-advisory-R3-homK7V and .oxlint-advisoryuMi3MP folders were removed
by the real sweep; the true no-dash form .oxlint-probe<rand> stayed. The
sweep deletes untracked data without confirmation, and its comment says
"matches the exact prefix" (:149), so the behavior contradicts the comment.
Fix owner Green, one line: require the character after '.oxlint-adv' to be
'-' or a digit, or list the exact seeded prefixes. The r3 b pin flips.

F2r2 and F3r2 stay accepted residuals: r2 a and r2 d still pass at this
HEAD and pin them (the S3 adversarial filter selects both). No CONTEST
item was routed back to this round.

